{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvtM6KKQYjv6r8eNTLs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EMqc1jfe4ac94RStc9XxEA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat engine/API.md","description":"Read the engine API card"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3654,"cache_read_input_tokens":46867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3654},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa","uuid":"bbbb5d14-054b-45be-94f1-38b558b04da0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:00:19.375Z","request_id":"req_011CghvtLniePy285T6VmX84","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EMqc1jfe4ac94RStc9XxEA":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055947__x9a2bbb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-055947 && cat engine/API.md","description":"Read the engine API card"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01EMqc1jfe4ac94RStc9XxEA":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055947__x9a2bbb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-055947"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EMqc1jfe4ac94RStc9XxEA","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (66KB). Full output saved to: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-build--20261104-055947--x9a2bbb-work/e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa/tool-results/bnikhn08d.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# my-3D2dge API card (v0.85.2)\n\nmy-3D2dge (\"My 3D 2D Game Engine\") is a general-purpose retro-modern 2D game engine built for AI models. Use it to port, remaster, reimagine and remix games from the 8-bit to 64-bit eras (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1), or to make spiritual successors to them. Everything is drawn by code: no image or sound files. Characters are 3D skeletons drawn as pixel art, and the camera can be any classic 2D view.\n\n**Start from a kit:** each genre has one, a complete small game written to be copied (the Genre playbook below names it). In a single file it sits between `GAME START` and `GAME END`: the starter's shell (the game, its title menu, the proof), the slice and the start; a genre kit holds one slice, `dist/my-3d2dge.html` every one and the ANIMATION LAB (how each animation is driven). In the handoff package each kit's game is `kits/<id>.js`, readable. **To make a game, change the slice into yours, with its own title, play and game-over scenes, and delete the starter's menu and the slices you do not use. The engine is yours to change too:** fix, extend or rewrite any of it as you see fit.\n\n**Looking a name up:** grep `API-INDEX.md` (every public name, one line; members are filed under instance names: `rig.`, `talk.`, `mover.`, `flow.`, `map.`), not the engine's source. It, the guide (`AI_GUIDE.md`) and the tools are in the handoff package (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/handoff/) and the repository.\n\n## Quick start (a complete game)\n```js\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp } = E;            // always start like this\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', view: 'threequarter' });\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['##########', '#@...s...#', '#..##....#', '#........#', '##########'],\n  legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero', 's': 'slime' },  // number = wall type, string = spawn tag\n  types: { 1: { h: 30, top: '#57506a', side: '#3d3750' } },\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa","uuid":"5e43b243-84ae-4066-b4f4-704f60866fb1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:00:19.405Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# my-3D2dge API card (v0.85.2)\n\nmy-3D2dge (\"My 3D 2D Game Engine\") is a general-purpose retro-modern 2D game engine built for AI models. Use it to port, remaster, reimagine and remix games from the 8-bit to 64-bit eras (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1), or to make spiritual successors to them. Everything is drawn by code: no image or sound files. Characters are 3D skeletons drawn as pixel art, and the camera can be any classic 2D view.\n\n**Start from a kit:** each genre has one, a complete small game written to be copied (the Genre playbook below names it). In a single file it sits between `GAME START` and `GAME END`: the starter's shell (the game, its title menu, the proof), the slice and the start; a genre kit holds one slice, `dist/my-3d2dge.html` every one and the ANIMATION LAB (how each animation is driven). In the handoff package each kit's game is `kits/<id>.js`, readable. **To make a game, change the slice into yours, with its own title, play and game-over scenes, and delete the starter's menu and the slices you do not use. The engine is yours to change too:** fix, extend or rewrite any of it as you see fit.\n\n**Looking a name up:** grep `API-INDEX.md` (every public name, one line; members are filed under instance names: `rig.`, `talk.`, `mover.`, `flow.`, `map.`), not the engine's source. It, the guide (`AI_GUIDE.md`) and the tools are in the handoff package (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/handoff/) and the repository.\n\n## Quick start (a complete game)\n```js\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp } = E;            // always start like this\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', view: 'threequarter' });\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['##########', '#@...s...#', '#..##....#', '#........#', '##########'],\n  legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero', 's': 'slime' },  // number = wall type, string = spawn tag\n  types: { 1: { h: 30, top: '#57506a', side: '#3d3750' } },\n  floorTex: (x, y) => E.tex.flagstone(x, y, { stones: ['#4b4559', '#554f64'].map(E.hex), mortar: E.hex('#221e2b'), hi: E.hex('#6f6782'), lo: E.hex('#322d3e'), speck: E.hex('#2a2634') })\n});\ngame.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v);\nconst s = map.find('hero'), hero = new E.Body({ x: s.x, y: s.y, r: 5 });\nconst rig = new E.Humanoid({ hat: 'pointed' });\ngame.start({\n  update(dt) {\n    const m = game.input.move(), d = game.view.screenDirToGround(m[0], m[1]);\n    hero.vx = d[0] * 80; hero.vy = d[1] * 80; hero.update(dt, map);\n    if (Math.hypot(d[0], d[1]) > .1) hero.facing = Math.atan2(d[1], d[0]);\n    rig.update(dt, { x: hero.x, y: hero.y, z: hero.z, vx: hero.vx, vy: hero.vy, facing: hero.facing || 0 });\n    game.focus(hero.x, hero.y, 10);                // the camera looks here: call every update\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    map.drawFloor(r); r.shadow(hero.x, hero.y, 5); map.queueWalls(r);\n    r.actor(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    r.text('HELLO', 4, 4, '#ffffff');              // HUD text in screen pixels\n  }\n});\n})();\n```\n\n## Look target (read this before drawing anything)\nAim above SNES, level with the best PS1 / N64 2D games (Symphony of the Night, Metal Slug, Legend of Mana, Klonoa). Games that skip these steps look like Atari games. **Every game should use all of them:**\n1. **Resolution** `res: 'ps1'` (320x240) or `'snes'`, with `expand: true` so it fills any screen (anchor the HUD to `r.W` / `r.H`), and characters 40-60 px tall: `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3 })` (HD style is the default: shaded volumetric limbs, outfits, hair).\n2. **Dress the character**: an `outfit`, `hair`, a `hat`, `armor`, a `cape`, `sleeves` (Characters), and a real palette in `colors` (never leave the defaults on everyone).\n3. **Backdrop behind every side-view level**: `const bg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night')` then `bg.draw(r)` first in `draw` (a ground view's floor runs on to the screen's edges: `map.outside`). Presets: `day dusk night castle-night city-night desert forest ocean cave space`, or your own `{ sky, sun | moon, stars, starsY: .7, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, fill }] }` (`starsY` = how far down the stars reach; a layer but clouds, fog and stalactites fills the screen below its skyline unless `fill: false`).\n4. **Textured tiles**: PlatformMap styles `stone` (with `moss`), `brick`, `wood`, `metal`, `ground` (with `flower`), `block`, `pipe`, `bonus`; TileMap floors from `E.tex.*`, TileMap walls with `face: 'brick' | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge'` and tops with `roof: 'tiles' | 'slab' | 'leaves' | 'grass'` (a village = timber and plaster houses with tile roofs, hedges, rock cliffs).\n5. **Props in every room** (3-8 per screen): `r.prop(name, x, y, z, { size, color, light: true })` with `torch candle candelabra chandelier brazier window banner pillar statue crate barrel chest pot sign fence lamp door tree pine bush flowers grass rock crystal bones skull vines cobweb lantern streetlamp awning hydrant trashcan firedrum sandbags cactus palm mushroom`. Flames animate, glow and can light the scene. `chest` / `door` take `{ open: true }`, `pillar` takes `{ broken: true }`, `window` is a gothic rose window with lead cames (`colors: [...]` for the glass, `size: 2-3` for a cathedral); hang `vines`, `cobweb`, `lantern` with `{ anchor: 'top' }`. With heroes at size 1.2+, give the scene `propSize: 1.4` (or set `E.style.propSize`) so props match them.\n6. **Effects on every hit**: `particles.explosion(x, y, z, size)`, `smoke`, `fire`, `glints`, `sparks`, `game.flash(color, s)`, `game.freeze`, `game.shake`.\n7. **Color**: `E.tones(hex)` gives `{ deep, sh, base, lt, hi }` hue-shifted shades and `E.ramp(hex, n)` a palette ramp. Shade everything you draw yourself with them (shadow side `sh`, lit edge `lt`, a `hi` sparkle).\n8. **Typography**: the default font is a 5x7 proportional font with lower case. Titles: `E.font.title(g, 'NAME', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: [...], align: 'center' })`. HUD text: `{ shadow: '#000', outline: false }` or `gradient: [top, bottom]`. `font: 'tiny'` is the old 3x5 font.\n9. **Light every scene**: `game.lights.enabled = true; game.lights.ambient = .5` in a scene's `enter`, then each draw a few lights where light comes from (`r.prop('lamp', x, y, 0, { light: true })`, `game.lights.add(x, y, z, 60, .9, { color })`): dusk, torchlight and glows give depth. It looks the same in every browser and check; `game.enableGPU({ map })` adds shadows in ground views, and falls back to it.\n10. **Faces in dialog**: `talk.say(lines, { name: 'MIRA', portrait: miraRig })` puts a live close-up of that Humanoid (blinking, hair, hat) beside every line. `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40)` draws one anywhere (HUD, RPG party windows).\n\n## Coordinates: what x, y, z mean in each view\nWorld units: one tile = 16. **z is always up.** Game logic never stores screen pixels.\n\n| View | Looks like | Ground plane | Use for levels | Move with |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `'iso'` (yaw 45, pitch 30) | Diablo, Landstalker | x/y ground, z up | `E.TileMap` | `E.Body` |\n| `'threequarter'` (pitch 55) | Zelda LttP, Stardew | x right, y down the screen | `E.TileMap` | `E.Body` |\n| `'topdown'` (pitch 80) | GTA 1, Hotline Miami | x right, y down | `E.TileMap` | `E.Body` |\n| `'brawler'` (pitch 25) | Final Fight, 2.5D | x right, y into the screen | `E.TileMap` or `E.PlatformMap` | `E.Body` or `E.Platformer` |\n| `'side'` (pitch 0) | Mario, Mega Man | **x right, z up, y = 0 (depth)** | `E.PlatformMap` | `E.Platformer` |\n| `'overhead'` (pitch 90, scale 1) | 1942, Galaga, Pac-Man | x = screen x px, y = screen y px | none, or a TileMap | your own x/y, or `E.Body` |\n\n- In `'side'` the screen shows x (right) and z (up). **y is depth and is normally 0.** Focus the camera with `game.focus(hero.x, 0, hero.z + 24)`.\n- In ground views, the screen direction the player pushes becomes a world direction through `game.view.screenDirToGround(mx, my)`.\n- `r.actor(x, y, z, (g, ox, oy) => ...)` calls your function with `(ox, oy)` = the buffer pixel where world point (x, y, z) lands. Draw the character around that point.\n\n## Rules\n1. Keep game logic in world units, and use `dt` everywhere. `update(dt)` runs in exact fixed steps: every 1/120 s of real time is one step of `dt = 1/120 * game.timeScale`, the same at any refresh rate (`game.alpha` = the part of a step left over).\n2. Draw only with `E.px.*`, `E.font`, `E.ui`, sprites, props and the `r.*` helpers. Never use `ctx.arc`, `ctx.stroke`, `ctx.fillText` or canvas gradients on the game buffer (they blur pixels). For translucency and glow use `px.blend(g, alpha, 'add' | 'multiply' | 'screen' | 'normal', () => {...})`, `px.polyDither`, `px.ddisc`, `r.glowDisc` and `r.shadow`: they use stepped alpha and blend modes like PS1 / SNES hardware (or dithering with `E.style.trans = 'dither'` for an NES / Genesis look).\n3. Anything that can overlap anything else goes through `r.actor`, `r.sprite` or `r.queue` (depth sorted). Backgrounds (`r.sky`, `map.drawFloor`, `level.draw`) come first in `draw`.\n4. Read input only in `update`. Use `pressed(a)` for one-shot actions (menus, jumps, shots), `down(a)` for held actions, and `buffered(a)` + `consume(a)` for forgiving combat input.\n5. Animate characters from continuous values (velocity, timers, easing): the rigs, not frame lists.\n6. Colors are `'#rrggbb'` (or `'#rgb'`) strings.\n7. Put the whole game in one IIFE `(() => { ... })();` between the markers, and start it with `game.start(...)`.\n\n## Common mistakes (check these first)\n- Nothing on screen: the camera looks at the wrong place. Use `game.follow(hero)` once (in the scene's `enter`), or call `game.focus(...)` every update. In side view the hero has y = 0.\n- Walls or level missing: you forgot `map.drawFloor(r)` + `map.queueWalls(r)` (TileMap) or `level.draw(r)` (PlatformMap).\n- Using a TileMap for a side-scroller. Side-scrollers use `E.PlatformMap` + `E.Platformer`.\n- HUD drawn in world coordinates. Use `r.text(...)` or `r.overlay(g => ...)` with screen pixels (`r.W`, `r.H`).\n- An old key layout: platformers want `input: 'PLATFORMER'` (Space jumps), shooters `input: 'SHMUP'` (Space fires).\n- Errors show in a red box on screen and in the console. Fix the first one first.\n\n## Game\n`new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', view, views, res, expand, input, bg })`\n- `res`: `'nes'` 256x240, `'snes'` 256x224, `'genesis'` 320x224, `'gb'` 160x144, `'gba'` 240x160, `'ps1'` / `'n64'` 320x240, `'wide'` 400x225, or `[w, h]`. Fixed pixels: whole-number scaling on a desktop screen, the largest fit on a phone (Settings, Pixel scaling). Leave it out for an adaptive size.\n- `expand: true`: full screen at any shape, no bars. `res` becomes the least the screen shows and `r.W` x `r.H` grows to fill the window (a 16:9 monitor shows about 427x240 of `'ps1'`, a phone held upright about 320x690). Anchor the HUD to `r.W` and `r.H`, and give the level something to show in the extra space (more of it, a backdrop, a HUD deck under it on a tall screen). `expand: { maxW, maxH }` caps the growth. A scene may set it too.\n- Adaptive size: `minW` / `minH` set the scale (the screen shows at least that many pixels), `maxW` / `maxH` cap the view (the rest is letterboxed). `portrait: { maxH: 1000 }` overrides them while the screen is taller than wide, so a phone held upright (9:16) is filled instead of showing a band across its middle. `game.screen.portrait` says which way it is.\n- `input`: `'DEFAULT'` (top-down action), `'PLATFORMER'`, `'SHMUP'`, `'THIRDPERSON'`, or your own `{ action: ['KeyQ', 'Pad0'] }`.\n- `views`: the views your game supports; `game.nextView()` cycles them (bind it to a key).\n- Start: `game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) })`, or with scenes (below).\n- Methods: `follow(obj, { z: 16, lead: 20 })` (camera tracks it automatically), `focus(x, y, z)` (or aim it yourself every update), `setView(id)`, `nextView()`, `freeze(s)` (hit-stop: `update` waits; `game.hitstop` is the time left), `shake(n)`, `after(s, fn)`, `every(s, fn)` (timers in game time, return `{ cancel() }`), `mouseGround()`, `go(scene, data)`, `enableGPU({ map })`.\n- Fields: `W`, `H` (screen pixels), `time`, `real`, `timeScale` (0.25 = slow motion), `paused`, `input`, `audio`, `particles`, `lights`, `view`, `errors`, `cam`. `game.fail('my power', err)` reports an error in your code (logged, in `errors`, on the error panel) and plays on.\n- Camera zoom and turn: `game.setZoom(1.5)` (.5 .. 3; everything drawn by the engine re-rasterizes crisply, the HUD stays), `game.rotateView(45)` (ground views only), `game.resetCamera()` (to the scene's zoom), `game.zoom`, `game.yaw`, `game.note('ZOOM 2x')` (a short notice at the top of the screen; `game.shownNote` is the one showing). Custom painters can read `r.view.zoom` (undefined at 1x) to scale their own art.\n- The player's zoom: a scene's `camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, tall: 1.5 }` lets the player zoom within `zoom` from `start` (wheel, `-` `=`, pinch, Settings; `false`: none; `AI_GUIDE.md`, Camera).\n- Tests and tools: `new E.Game({ headless: true })` (the default in Node: no screen, sound or DOM; `draw` is skipped) or `{ loop: false }` runs only by `game.advance(seconds, { draw })` (exact fixed steps at once); `input.tap(action)` presses for one step, `input.hold(action, on)`; `game.debug = { snapshot() {...} }` is your game's handle (`tools/check.mjs` prints it); `game.stop()`, `start()` (resumes), `dispose()`.\n- Sessions: `?record=1`, then the pause menu's Save session; `node tools/replay.mjs session.json` replays it exactly, headless (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Sessions).\n- Camera: `cam.offset = [dx, dy]` sits the focus that many screen pixels from the centre (above a phone's touch buttons: `[0, -60]`); `cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v)` keeps it inside the level (in side views a level shorter than the screen sits on the bottom edge; `cam.align = 'center'` to change); `cam.room = [160, 128]` moves screen by screen (Zelda, Metroid) and `cam.moving` is true while it slides; `cam.smooth` = lag in seconds (0 = locked to the target, no lag); `cam.window = [48, 24]` a dead zone the focus moves in before the camera follows; `cam.snapY = true` follows a followed body's height only when it lands (side-scrollers); `cam.frame([p1, p2], { margin, zoom: [.5, 1] })` keeps them all in view, zooming out as they part (`frame(null)` stops); `cam.free = { keys, edge: 10, drag, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }` a free camera (strategy, sims): keys or a pad's stick, the screen's edge, a drag pan it (a finger pans by its drag, never as the touch stick), a zoom goes toward the pointer or the pinch, in every view and turn.\n\n## Scenes (title, play, game over)\n```js\ngame.start({ scene: 'title', scenes: {\n  title: { update(dt) { if (game.input.pressed('start')) game.go('play', { level: 1 }); },\n           draw(r) { r.sky(['#101848', '#402a70']); r.text('PRESS START', r.W / 2, 100, '#fff', { align: 'center', scale: 2 }); } },\n  play: { pausable: true, view: 'side', input: 'PLATFORMER', res: 'snes', views: ['side', 'brawler'], touch: ['jump', 'attack'],\n          enter(data) { /* build the level */ }, exit() {}, update(dt) {}, draw(r) {} }\n} });\n```\n`game.go(name, data)` switches before the next step, through a short dithered fade (`game.fadeTime`; `{ fade: 0 }` cuts; `{ fade: 'wipe' | 'iris' | 'mosaic' | 'swirl' | 'dissolve' | 'white', seconds: .4, at: hero }` a transition, a plain fade under reduce motion); timers and particles are cleared. `pausable: true` lets Escape / P / Start pause it and opens the pause menu (below). `view`, `views`, `input`, `res`, `expand`, `touch`, `propSize` are applied on entry. A scene's `back()` takes a phone's back gesture first (return true when it went back somewhere: a sub-menu closed).\n\n## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\n- Tweens (Phaser's): `game.tween(door, { y: 40 }, .5, { ease: 'outBack', delay, repeat, yoyo, onDone, keep })` eases numbers on game time: paused with the game, slowed by `timeScale`, ended by a scene change unless `keep`. Returns `{ done, cancel() }`. `E.ease` has Penner's set: `linear`, `inSine` `outSine` `inOutSine`, `inQuad` `outQuad` `inOutQuad`, the same for `Cubic`, `Back`, `Elastic`, `Bounce`.\n- Scripts (Unity's coroutines) for cutscenes, boss patterns, wave timelines, tutorials:\n```js full-script\ngame.script(function* () {\n  yield 1;                                   // seconds of game time\n  yield E.until(() => door.open);            // a condition\n  yield game.tween(boss, { y: 80 }, 1.5);    // a tween (or another script, or a generator) finishing\n  for (let w = 0; w < 3; w++) { spawnWave(w); yield E.any([8, () => enemies.length === 0]); }\n});\n```\n  `E.all([...])` waits for all; a bare `yield` waits one step. It runs at once to its first `yield`, the same at any refresh rate; `{ keep: true }` outlives the scene; `.cancel()`, `.done`, `.value`.\n- Paths: `const p = new E.Path([[x, y, z], ...], { closed, smooth: 'catmull' })`: `p.length`, `p.at(d)` (`{ x, y, z, angle }` by distance along: moving platforms, dives, rails), `p.nearest(x, y)` (a racer's progress), `p.draw(r)` to see it.\n- Weather: `game.weather = { kind: 'rain' | 'snow' | 'ash' | 'leaves' | 'sand', amount: .8, wind: .3, lightning: .2 }` (null: clear) falls through the world in every view, settles or splashes, flashes and thunders; cosmetic only (its own random stream), and it ends with the scene: set it in `enter`.\n- Wrap-around (Asteroids): `x = E.wrap(x, 0, W)`, `E.wrapDiff(a, b, W)` (the short way across the seam), and `wrap: [W, H]` on `r.sprite` or `r.actor` draws a copy across each edge.\n\n## Standard features (every game has them: don't build your own)\nWith no code: a **pause menu** on pausable scenes (Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title; keys, mouse, gamepad and touch), **settings** saved per game (`game.settings`: volume, music, effects, mute, reduce motion, screen shake and flashes, pixel scaling, a screen filter: clean, scanlines or CRT, the frame rate: Auto, 60 or Full, and its readout), **controls** the player rebinds (conflicts said first; dead zone, invert aim, button symbols, vibration; touch button side, size, opacity), **full screen** (a phone's first tap and each game started by a tap, a top-right button, the menu; turning it off is remembered), a **menu button** at the top right (on a touch screen it stays in play: it is the touch START), a **way out** of every menu screen (close, back, a sideways swipe), the **back gesture** stepping back in the game (`game.back()`: a menu screen closes, play pauses) before it leaves the page, **pausing** when the page is hidden or the controller unplugs, and a page set up for phones (safe areas, no scrolling, zooming or pull to refresh on the canvas).\n- Adjust: `new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }, { key: 'difficulty', options: ['Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard'], value: 'Normal' }], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: false }, quit: 'title' } })`, then read `game.settings.hints`. Leave parts out: `menu: false` (your own pause), `fullscreen: 'button' | false`, `corner: false`, `backGesture: false`, `autoPause: false`. `game.cornerArea()`: where the corner's buttons cover the screen (or null): keep a HUD clear of it.\n- Save slots (`game.saves`): three slots and an autosave, each with its place, level and time played. `game.saves.write = () => ({ data, place, level })` and `read = save => {...}`; then `save(slot)` (0, 1, 2 or `'auto'`), `load(slot)`, `copy(a, b)`, `erase(slot)`, `autosave()`, `list()`, `latest()` (a title's Continue). `menu: { saves: true }` (or `{ slots, version, migrate(data, from) }`) puts Save (while `saves.canSave`: a save point) and Load in the pause menu, and `saves.show('save' | 'load')` opens the screen from your own menu. Blocked storage keeps them for the visit.\n- Prompts: `game.input.label('jump')` is that action's key or button on the player's device, after rebinding ('Space', 'A', '✕'). A canvas title's OPTIONS: `game.menu('settings')`. From code: `game.settings.set(key, v)`, `game.fullscreen.toggle()` (from a key, click or tap), `game.pause(reason)`, `game.resume()`.\n- **Boot**: heavy setup in steps behind a boot screen, and a report for any error before play: `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot: { title, steps: [['Building the city', () => { map = build(); }]] } })` (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Boot).\n\n## Input: `game.input`\n- Actions in every preset: `up down left right` (WASD, arrows, d-pad), `start` (Enter, Start), `pause` (Escape, P, Start), `confirm` (Enter, Space, J, Z, pad A), `cancel` (Escape, Backspace, X, K, pad B).\n- DEFAULT adds `attack` (J, X, click), `dash` (Space, Shift, K), `skill` (L, E, right click), `jump` (Z). PLATFORMER: `jump` (Space, Z, K, pad A), `attack` (X, J, click), `dash` (Shift, C, L), `skill`. SHMUP: `fire` (Space, Z, J, click), `bomb` (X, K). THIRDPERSON: `sprint` (Shift), `jump` (Space), `crouch` (C, Ctrl), `interact` (E, F), `attack` (J), `block` (K), `dodge` (L), `use` (Q), `map` (M, Tab).\n- `down(a)`, `pressed(a)`, `released(a)`, `repeat(a, delay, rate)` (menus), `buffered(a, win)` + `consume(a)`, `consumeAll()`, `anyPressed()`, `move()` (screen direction `[x, y]`, length up to 1), `use(preset)`, `touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'])`, `touchSet('confirm', 'TALK', near)` (a context button: relabel it, or hide it while it has nothing to do).\n- Moves: `input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing })` is true on the step a quarter circle forward and punch ends (numpad notation, mirrored when `facing` is -1: `'623'`, `'41236'`); `input.sequence(['up', 'up', 'down', 'down+right', 'attack'], { window: .5 })` any run of inputs (a cheat code); `input.history` the last second of them (`{ t, dir, pressed }`, for an input display).\n- Players (two to four on one machine): `game.players` is `[game.input, ...]`, each an input with this API, its `player` number, `name` (`'P2'`), `color` (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) and device. `game.allowJoin({ max: 2, onJoin: (input, n) => {} })` lets them in: Start on a free gamepad, or 2 on the keyboard (player 2 takes its right half: arrows, `.` `/` `,` and the numpad; player 1 keeps WASD with F G H); `game.addPlayer({ pad: 0 })` or `({ keys: 'right' })`, `game.removePlayer(p)`. Prompts, the pause (P2 PAUSED), a lost controller and the Controls screen are per player. One screen: `cam.frame(heroes)`. Split: `game.splitScreen(2, { follow: [h1, h2], layout: 'auto' })` (`'columns'`, `'rows'`, `'grid'`; up to 4) draws the scene once per viewport (`r.viewport` is `{ i, x, y, w, h }`), then `scene.hud(r)` once over the whole screen; `game.viewports[i].follow(t)` or `.focus(x, y)`.\n- `clear()` releases held inputs, pending presses, virtual sticks and touch buttons; focus loss does this automatically. `suppress(a)` blocks an action for the current tick; `suppressCode('Mouse0')` lets a HUD widget consume that mouse button while other devices bound to the action still work.\n- Controller settings: `deadzone` (default `.18`, radial and rescaled), `invertAimY`, `lastDevice` (the index has the rest). The left stick and the touch stick, pushed past halfway, press `up` / `down` / `left` / `right` as the d-pad does (menus, dialog choices, ladders); bind `PadAxisUp/Down/Left/Right` to your own menu actions for the same.\n- Touch settings: `touchEnabled`, `stickSide` (`'left'` or `'right'`), `stickRadius` (CSS pixels), `touchFilter(event)` (return false to reserve a canvas tap for UI). `touchArea()`: where the touch buttons cover the screen (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }` in screen pixels, or null): keep a prompt clear of it, as a bottom `E.Dialog` does by itself. `clicked()`: where a click or tap on the canvas landed (`[x, y]` in screen pixels) for the step after it, else null, for HUD buttons of your own; `pointer()`: the mouse in screen pixels; `drag()`: how far the stick's finger moved this step (`[dx, dy]`, or null), to steer one to one; `steer = 'drag'`: a finger anywhere steers, no stick drawn (`stickOn`: a finger is on it). `zones = [{ x0, y0, x1, y1, act }]` (fractions of the canvas): a finger in one holds its act until it lifts, no stick (a pinball's halves, a rhythm game's lanes). Gestures (a mouse or one finger, screen pixels): `box()` → `{ x0, y0, x1, y1, done }` (a left drag; on touch a long press, then a drag), `longPress()`, `doubleTap()`, `pan()` → `[dx, dy]` (a finger's drag on open ground, a middle or right drag), `zoomPoint()`; `feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch, button, id })` plays a pointer in a test. `bindButtons(root)` wires `[data-act]` elements with independent pointer tracking and cancellation cleanup.\n\n## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\n- Background: `r.sky(['#top', '#mid', '#bottom'])`, `r.starfield({ count, speed, dir: 'down' | 'left' })`.\n- Depth sorted: `r.actor(x, y, z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view), { flash: '#ffffff', flashMix: .75, alpha, xray, outline, ghost, emissive, every, key })` (the flash tints over the sprite so shading shows: `flashMix` .5 by default, 1 solid; `every: 2, key: npc` redraws a background character every other frame; actors up to about 250 px tall), `r.sprite(x, y, z, sprite, { flip, anchor: 'bottom' | 'center', glow, flash })`, `r.queue(x, y, z, g => {...}, { bias })`, `r.actorNow(...)` (as `r.actor`, drawn at once over what is drawn so far), `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)` (inside a queue function). `{ pick: unit }` on any of them (and `r.shape`), then `r.pick(sx, sy)` → what the last frame drew under a screen point, front to back.\n- Floor marks: `r.shadow(x, y, radius, alpha, color, surfaceZ)`, `r.decal(g => r.groundArc(...))`, `r.groundDisc`, `r.groundRing`, `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n, z)`.\n- On top, unlit, screen pixels: `r.text(str, x, y, color, { align, scale, outline })`, `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color)`, `r.overlay(g => {...})`.\n- `r.w(x, y, z)` = buffer pixel of a world point. `r.W`, `r.H`, `r.ix`, `r.iy` (pass to dither functions), `r.view`, `r.visible(x, y, z)`.\n- X-ray: `r.actor(..., { xray: true })` shows the actor's hidden part, a translucent tint with a 1-px outline (a checker in `E.style.trans = 'dither'`), wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high (22; `hides: true | false` says otherwise) or anything queued with `{ hides: true }` is drawn in front of it; not by one rising less than 8 above its feet (the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall). `xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors: true }`: with `actors` other bodies in front hide it too (a hero stays findable in a crowd). Afterimages: `ghost: { color, life, alpha, owner }`; `owner` (the actor's `{x, y, z}`) keeps a trail left nearer the camera sorted behind the live body.\n- Glowing things you draw yourself: `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, { emissive: true })` is drawn again after lighting so darkness never dims it (flames, lasers, magic, neon). It still hides behind whatever stands in front of it: walls and `r.actor` bodies do this on their own, and any other queued draw can join them with `{ solid: true }`. (Canvas lighting builds a depth-ordered mask for this; `game.r.glowMask = false` skips it on slow machines.)\n\n## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\n- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`, `dot`, `line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, width)`, `disc(g, x, y, r, c)`, `ell`, `poly(g, pts, c)`, `polyDither(g, pts, c, 0..1, r.ix, r.iy)`, `ddisc`, `sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip)` (or `{ flip, rot, scale }`), `glow(g, 0..1)` (GPU glow for what follows).\n- Sprites from strings (for coins, bullets, ships, icons, NES-style enemies): `const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }, scale)`. `.` and space are transparent. Frames: `const walk = E.anim([f1, f2, f3], 8, { pingpong })` (or one sheet: `E.anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 })`), drawn with `r.sprite(x, y, z, walk, { t })`. `r.sprite(..., { rot: angle, scale })` turns and scales in whole pixels (cached in 16 steps a turn; `steps: 32`); `E.recolor(spr, { '#3a8a4a': '#8a3a4a' })` swaps a palette.\n- Font (5x7 proportional with lower case; `font: 'tiny'` for 3x5): `E.font.text(g, str, x, y, color, { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font })`, `E.font.title(g, str, x, y, { scale, colors, outline, depth, depthColor, align })`, `E.font.width(str, opts)`, `E.font.lineHeight(opts)`, `E.font.wrap(str, maxW, opts)`. Glyphs: ASCII plus `♥ ★ ← → ↑ ↓ • × ♪ ▸ ©`.\n- UI (inside `r.overlay(g => ...)`): `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, gradient, alpha })` (a gradient window like Final Fantasy; `bg` can be `[top, bottom]`, `gradient: false` for flat, `alpha: .6` for a see-through HUD panel), `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, color)`, `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max)` (half hearts allowed), `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg, frame, cape: false, weapon: false, tint: '#808080' })` (character close-up; it stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down; `tint` greys out a KO'd hero).\n- Dialog: `const talk = new E.Dialog(game)`; `talk.say(['Line one.', 'Page two.'], { name: 'ELDER', portrait: elderRig, onDone, choices: ['YES', 'NO'], onChoice(i) })` (choices show on the last page: the keys, or a tap or click on one, pick); in update `if (talk.update(dt)) return;` (true while a modal box is open: play waits); in draw `talk.draw(r)`. `portrait` takes a Humanoid (live close-up; `portraitSize: 40`, `portraitOpts: { zoom, turn }`) or a function `(g, x, y, size) => {...}`. Radio chatter during play: `talk.say('Enemy fighters ahead!', { name, portrait, auto: 2.5, modal: false })` turns its pages and closes by itself while the game keeps running. Per line: `place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom'`, `y` (pixels) and `alpha` (see-through box). A portrait's mouth moves while its text types. `new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars })`; `talk.close()`, `talk.open`. Markup in the text: `{c=#ffd36a}gold{/c}` a color, `{w=.5}` a pause, `{s=12}slowly{/s}` letters a second, `{shake}..{/shake}`, `{wave}..{/wave}`, `{$name}` a value f","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-build--20261104-055947--x9a2bbb-work/e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa/tool-results/bnikhn08d.txt","persistedOutputSize":67603},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EMqc1jfe4ac94RStc9XxEA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvtXfKGeQvwU1RkB33f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017MucYqneKYGcwpDGxngvMU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1,400p engine/kits/sports.js","description":"Read first part of the sports kit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1256,"cache_read_input_tokens":50521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1256},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa","uuid":"9123b47e-80f5-4516-86aa-d492e1dc62dc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:00:21.174Z","request_id":"req_011CghvtXKjBzq2LLMXQdkoV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017MucYqneKYGcwpDGxngvMU":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055947__x9a2bbb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-055947 && sed -n 1,400p engine/kits/sports.js","description":"Read first part of the sports kit"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_017MucYqneKYGcwpDGxngvMU":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055947__x9a2bbb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-055947"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017MucYqneKYGcwpDGxngvMU","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (34KB). Full output saved to: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-build--20261104-055947--x9a2bbb-work/e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa/tool-results/bxjpl01e9.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n// The SPORTS kit's game (two against two in a walled cage, up to four players: a ball that bounces and curls, passes, lobs, shots on a meter, formations, a match clock; Sensible Soccer and NBA Jam), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/68-sports.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. sports.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs sports runs it headless.\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa","uuid":"5b0b24b4-8fbd-42f0-b236-fe73a2d889d4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:00:21.195Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// The SPORTS kit's game (two against two in a walled cage, up to four players: a ball that bounces and curls, passes, lobs, shots on a meter, formations, a match clock; Sensible Soccer and NBA Jam), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/68-sports.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. sports.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs sports runs it headless.\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n * expand: the picture fills the window, any shape, with no bars: at least 320 x 240 (a slice's res), more on the long side */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d' });\nconst P = game.particles, L = game.lights, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {};\nlet gpu = null;                               // WebGPU lighting, used by the adventure slice only\nconst best = (k, v) => { const old = E.store.get('best:' + k, 0); if (v > old) E.store.set('best:' + k, v); return Math.max(old, v); };\n// a prompt in the player's own controls, after rebinding: 'J Sword' on a keyboard, 'X Sword' on a pad, 'ATTACK Sword' (the\n// button's name) on a touch screen, where the buttons sit over the bottom corner: touch() says so, to move a prompt off it\nconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch';\n// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\nconst SLICES = [\n  { id: 'adventure', label: 'ADVENTURE', about: 'TOP-DOWN ACTION ADVENTURE', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'pointclick', label: 'POINT-AND-CLICK', about: 'RELIGHT THE LIGHTHOUSE ON GULL ROCK', family: 'ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING PLATFORMER', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'metroidvania', label: 'METROIDVANIA', about: 'A WORLD OF ROOMS, ITS MAP, ITS GATES', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'brawler', label: 'BRAWLER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING BEAT-EM-UP', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'fighting', label: 'FIGHTING', about: 'ONE ON ONE, BEST OF THREE', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'VERTICAL SHOOT-EM-UP', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'arcade', label: 'ARCADE', about: 'A CABINET OF THREE CLASSICS', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'pinball', label: 'PINBALL', about: 'ONE TABLE: RAMP, MULTIBALL, JACKPOT', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'kart', label: 'KART', about: 'MODE 7 KARTS, THREE LAPS', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'road', label: 'ROAD', about: 'A COAST ROAD AGAINST THE CLOCK', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'puzzle', label: 'PUZZLE', about: 'FALLING BLOCKS AND FALLING PAIRS', family: 'PUZZLE' },\n  { id: 'rhythm', label: 'RHYTHM', about: 'STEP UP! FOUR LANES, TWO SONGS', family: 'MUSIC' },\n  { id: 'rpg', label: 'RPG', about: 'A JOURNEY: TOWN, WORLD, CAVE, BATTLES', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'roguelike', label: 'ROGUELIKE', about: 'A CRYPT OF TEN GENERATED FLOORS', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'tactics', label: 'TACTICS', about: 'TAKE THE HILL FORT, TURN BY TURN', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'rts', label: 'RTS', about: 'GATHER GOLD, RAISE AN ARMY, BURN THEIR CAMP', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'artillery', label: 'ARTILLERY', about: 'TWO TEAMS OF THREE ON AN ISLAND THAT BLOWS APART', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'sim', label: 'SIM', about: 'BUILD A THEME PARK, KEEP THEM SMILING', family: 'SIMULATION' },\n  { id: 'stealth', label: 'STEALTH', about: 'ROOFTOP STEALTH AND PARKOUR', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'sports', label: 'SPORTS', about: 'TWO AGAINST TWO IN THE CAGE', family: 'SPORTS' },\n  { id: 'animlab', label: 'ANIMATION LAB', about: 'EVERY MOVE, SKIN AND VIEW', family: 'TOOLS' }\n];\n/* the camera: each slice's scene says how the player may zoom it, camera: { zoom: [min, max] | false, start, tall }: the\n   engine zooms it with the mouse wheel, - and =, a pinch on a phone and Settings, Camera zoom (the player's own, kept, on\n   top of the slice's start: tall on a phone held upright). Keys every slice shares besides: V changes the camera view,\n   [ and ] turn it (camera.rotate), 0 resets it (the player's zoom too), G toggles GPU lighting, M mutes */\nconst camOpt = () => (game.scene && game.scene.camera) || {};\naddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (e.repeat) return;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); game.note(game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW'); }\n  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }   // (resetCamera draws it at once)\n  else if ((e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') && camOpt().rotate) { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyM') A.mute();\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyG' && gpu) gpu.enabled = !gpu.enabled;\n});\n\n/* ---- TITLE: a lineup of HD heroes on a torch-lit castle ledge under a dusk sky. The ledge is wide enough for a wide\n * screen and sits on the screen's bottom edge whatever its height; the logo and menu hang from the top ---- */\nconst MID = 480, stage = new E.PlatformMap({ rows: ['S'.repeat(60), 'S'.repeat(60)], legend: { S: 1 },\n  types: { 1: { style: 'stone', side: '#6a5a78', moss: '#4a6a3a' } }, edges: 'open' });\nconst titleBg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night');\nconst HEROES = [   // six heroes, each dressed with the HD rig options\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hair: 'short', cape: { len: 6, width: 6, seg: 2.6 }, colors: { cloth: '#3a5ab0', cape: '#b02a3a', capeIn: '#5a1020', hair: '#e0b050', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3aa050' }, colors: { cloth: '#3aa050', pants: '#e8dcc0', hair: '#e0b040', trim: '#8a5a2a' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#e03a3a' }, colors: { cloth: '#f0f0f0', pants: '#2f5fd0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', hair: '#c8402a', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#e8e4dc', coat: '#d8d2c8', trim: '#b02a2a', belt: '#b02a2a', pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#3a2e2a' } }) }   // the stealth slice's hooded assassin\n];\nHEROES.forEach((h, i) => { h.x = MID + (i - 2.5) * 35; });\n// the corner's buttons (menu, full screen, the page's ? API) in game pixels: about 170 x 60 CSS pixels at the top right\nconst corner = () => { const S = game.screen, k = S.dpr / S.S; return [170 * k, 60 * k]; };\n// where a HUD's top-right corner ends: left of the corner's menu button while it stays there (a touch screen), else the edge\nconst cornerX = () => { const ca = touch() && game.cornerArea(); return ca && ca.y0 < 40 ? Math.floor(ca.x0) - 4 : game.W; };\n/* ---- THE PROOF (tools/kits-test.mjs runs each slice's twice and compares): proof(id, n, script, state, fresh) enters the\n * slice afresh on a game clock at 0, with Math.random seeded, runs n fixed steps of 1/120 s with script(i, key) pressing\n * keys (key.hold('right'), key.up('right'), key.tap('attack')), and gives a hash of what state() returns: the numbers that\n * say how the run went. fresh(), when given, runs first (seeded): it puts back what the slice keeps between visits. A\n * slice's run(n) is one (__game.scenes.adventure.run(600)): the same number every time ---- */\nconst proof = (id, n, script, state, fresh) => {\n  const was = Math.random, I = game.input, held = new Set();\n  const key = { hold: a => { held.add(a); I.hold(a); }, up: a => { held.delete(a); I.hold(a, false); }, tap: a => I.tap(a) };\n  Math.random = E.rng(7);\n  try {\n    if (fresh) fresh();\n    game.time = 0; game.timeScale = 1; game.go(id, null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { script(i, key); game.advance(1 / 120); }\n    const s = JSON.stringify(state()); let h = 2166136261;\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ s.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n    return h >>> 0;\n  } finally { for (const a of held) I.hold(a, false); Math.random = was; }\n};\n// a proof's walk: every `every` steps it lets go of the directions and holds the next of `dirs`\nconst walk = (i, key, dirs, every) => { if (i % every) return; for (const d of dirs) key.up(d); key.hold(dirs[(i / every) % dirs.length]); };\n// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does: any player's\nconst pickOnStart = m => { const P = game.players; if (P.some(I => I.pressed('start'))) { P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\n/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\nconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\nlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\nscenes.title = {\n  view: 'side', views: ['side', 'brawler'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter() { A.music('title'); game.resetCamera(); game.follow(null); game.cam.room = null; game.cam.bounds = null; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n    game.focus(MID, 0, 32 + (game.H / 2 - 42) / -game.view.bz);   // the ledge's top 42 px above the screen's bottom edge\n    const t = game.time;\n    HEROES.forEach((h, i) => {\n      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n      h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: 0, z: 32, facing: h.face, vx: 0, vy: 0, attack: swing, point: i === 3 && u < .6 });\n    });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    const [cw, ch] = corner(), top = r.W / 2 + 132 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;   // the logo drops below the corner's buttons where it would reach them (an upright phone)\n    titleMenu.y = 76 + top;\n    titleBg.draw(r);\n    stage.draw(r);\n    for (const x of [MID - 100, MID + 100]) r.prop('torch', x, 0, 32, { size: 1.3, light: false });\n    for (const x of [MID - 53, MID + 53]) r.prop('banner', x, -8, 64, { size: 1.1, color: '#8a1a2a' });\n    for (const h of HEROES) r.actor(h.x, 0, 32, (g, ox, oy) => h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, 12 + top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n      E.font.text(g, 'My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine', r.W / 2, 48 + top, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center', gradient: ['#ffffff', '#c8b8f0'], shadow: '#140c1c', outline: false });\n      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    });\n    titleMenu.draw(r);\n    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu'\n      : 'Arrows + Enter or click   V view   - = zoom   M mute';\n    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n  }\n};\n\n/* ---- GAME OVER: shared by every slice ---- */\nconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 118, onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? overMenu.from : 'title') });\nconst overBg = new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#12040c', '#3a0c1c', '#6a1a28'], moon: { x: .5, y: .3, r: 16, color: '#e8a0a0' }, stars: 30,\n  layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#2a0c16', y: .72, height: .3, parallax: 0 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a2a3a', y: .9, height: .12, parallax: 0, drift: 4 }] });\nscenes.over = {\n  view: 'side', input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter(d) { overMenu.from = d.from; overMenu.i = 0; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); game.follow(null); game.focus(0, 0, 0); if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n  draw(r) {   // centred on any screen\n    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 60; overMenu.y = y + 58;\n    overBg.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: '#3a0810' })); overMenu.draw(r);\n  }\n};\n\n/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 22  SPORTS  (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam, Tecmo Bowl).\n * Two against two in a walled cage, for up to four players: the GULLS against the RUST, two halves on the clock, a\n * golden goal if it ends level. The ball is a Body: it rolls, bounces off the ground and the boards, and curls.\n * KEYS: the stick runs; J passes (to the teammate the stick points at, led to where it is going), L lobs one over a\n * defender (its arc solved by E.arc to land at the teammate's feet), K held fills the shot meter and shoots on letting go\n * (the stick across the goal aims it; pushed sideways just after, it curls: aftertouch). Without the ball: J slides in\n * to tackle, K switches to the teammate nearer the ball. TOUCH: the stick, PASS, SHOOT (hold), LOB.\n * PLAYERS: MATCH is you against the CPU; VERSUS lets players 2 to 4 in (2 on the keyboard, or Start on a pad): player 2\n * takes the RUST, 3 and 4 the second of each side. The rest are run by formation: with the ball, the other one runs\n * ahead on the far side; without it, the nearer presses and the other covers the goal. Commentary on Dialog's radio.\n * Deep links: #sports/match (a match against the CPU), #sports/vs (VERSUS: players 2 to 4 join).\n * HOW IT WORKS: a TileMap cage (boards that cut low before the camera, nets), the ball and the players as E.Body, rigs\n * that kick and slide (E.Attack), E.arc for the lob, game.allowJoin for players; SPORTS.run(n) is the proof,\n * SPORTS.bot() plays a match through to its whistle and then a short one with four players.\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst SPORTS = (() => {\n  const A = game.audio, T = 16, FW = 36, FH = 22, ND = 2, GOAL = 5, BAR = 28, HALF = 60, GOLDEN = 45, PI = Math.PI;\n  /* ---- THE CAGE: a field of FW x FH tiles inside boards (cut low where they hide it), a goal in each end with its net,\n   * a stand of three tiers behind the north boards; built from rows: # boards, N net, . the field, : the net's floor,\n   * 1 2 3 the stand's tiers (back to front), , outside ---- */\n  const STAND = 3, COLS = ND + FW + 2 + ND, ROWS = STAND + FH + 2, MID = FH / 2, goalRow = r => r > MID - GOAL / 2 && r <= MID + GOAL / 2;\n  const rows = [];\n  for (let R = 0; R < ROWS; R++) {\n    let s = ''; const r = R - STAND;   // (the cage's own row)\n    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n      const field = c > ND && c <= ND + FW && r > 0 && r <= FH, endCol = c === ND || c === ND + FW + 1, net = (c < ND || c > ND + FW + 1);\n      if (r < 0) s += c >= ND && c <= ND + FW + 1 ? String(R + 1) : ',';\n      else if (field) s += '.';\n      else if (endCol && r > 0 && r <= FH) s += goalRow(r) ? '.' : '#';\n      else if ((r === 0 || r === FH + 1) && c >= ND && c <= ND + FW + 1) s += '#';\n      else if (net && goalRow(r)) s += c === 0 || c === COLS - 1 ? 'N' : ':';\n      else if (net && (goalRow(r + 1) || goalRow(r - 1))) s += 'N';\n      else s += ',';\n    }\n    rows.push(s);\n  }\n  const X0 = (ND + 1) * T, X1 = (ND + 1 + FW) * T, Y0 = (STAND + 1) * T, Y1 = (STAND + FH + 1) * T, CX = (X0 + X1) / 2, CY = (Y0 + Y1) / 2, GH = GOAL * T / 2;\n  // the pitch: mown stripes with the grass's own grain, painted lines a little worn (the halfway line, the centre circle,\n  // an arc before each goal), the nets' shadow on their floor, tarmac outside\n  const line = (x, y) => {\n    const d = Math.hypot(x - CX, y - CY), ex = Math.min(Math.abs(x - X0), Math.abs(x - X1)), ey = Math.min(Math.abs(y - Y0), Math.abs(y - Y1));\n    if (ex < 1.5 || ey < 1.5 || Math.abs(x - CX) < 1 || Math.abs(d - 48) < 1) return true;\n    for (const gx of [X0, X1]) if (Math.abs(Math.hypot(x - gx, y - CY) - 72) < 1 && Math.abs(x - gx) < 72) return true;\n    return false;\n  };\n  const floorTex = (x, y, tag) => {\n    const n = E.hash2(Math.floor(x), Math.floor(y)) - .5, m = E.noise2(x * .06, y * .06) * .5;\n    if (tag === 'net') { const mesh = Math.floor(x) % 4 === 0 || Math.floor(y) % 4 === 0; return mesh ? [30, 66, 36] : [44 + n * 10, 92 + n * 14, 50 + n * 10]; }\n    if (tag === 'out') return [44 + n * 18, 42 + n * 18, 50 + n * 18];\n    if (line(x, y)) { const w = 228 + n * 24 + m * 10; return [w, w + 4, w - 8]; }\n    const k = Math.floor((x - X0) / 32) % 2 ? 1 : 0, g = (k ? 140 : 106) + n * 34 + m * 24;   // (a stripe mown each way: lighter, darker)\n    return [g * .42, g, g * .46];\n  };\n  let map = null;\n  const makeMap = () => new E.TileMap({ rows, legend: { '#': 1, N: 2, 1: 5, 2: 4, 3: 3, '.': { floor: 'grass' }, ':': { floor: 'net' }, ',': { floor: 'out' } }, floorTex, outside: '#1e1c24', ao: 4,\n    types: { 1: { h: 26, cut: true, cutH: 6, face: 'plank', side: '#3a4a6a', top: '#d8dce8', line: '#2a3450' }, 2: { h: BAR + 4, face: 'none', side: '#b8bcc8', top: '#e0e4ec' },\n      3: { h: 34, face: 'stone', side: '#5a5468', top: '#6a6478' }, 4: { h: 44, face: 'stone', side: '#4e4a5e', top: '#5e586e' }, 5: { h: 54, face: 'stone', side: '#44405a', top: '#544e66' } } });\n  // the crowd: two on each tile of the stand, in their colors, bobbing; on a goal, those of the side that scored jump\n  const CROWD = [];\n  for (let R = 0; R < STAND; R++) for (let c = ND; c <= ND + FW + 1; c++) for (const dx of [4, 12]) {\n    const h = E.hash2(c * 3 + dx, R * 7 + 1), side = h < .5 ? 0 : 1;\n    CROWD.push({ x: c * T + dx, y: R * T + 9, z: [54, 44, 34][R], side, shirt: side ? ['#c8502a', '#e07040', '#a83a1a'][(h * 30 | 0) % 3] : ['#eef0f6', '#2a5ab8', '#8ab0f0'][(h * 30 | 0) % 3], skin: ['#e0b090', '#a87050', '#6a4028', '#f0c8a8'][(h * 50 | 0) % 4], ph: h * 9 });\n  }\n  /* ---- THE TEAMS: their colors, names and players; the ball ---- */\n  const TEAMS = [\n    { name: 'GULLS', colors: { cloth: '#eef0f6', pants: '#2a5ab8', boot: '#1e2030', belt: '#2a5ab8', trim: '#2a5ab8' }, chip: '#eef0f6', players: [['NOOR', '#3a2418', '#c89070'], ['BEX', '#e8c070', '#f0c8a8']] },\n    { name: 'RUST', colors: { cloth: '#c8502a', pants: '#2a2a30', boot: '#1a1a1e', belt: '#1a1a1e', trim: '#e8c070' }, chip: '#c8502a', players: [['DRAGO', '#1e1c1a', '#a87050'], ['KIT', '#6a3a22', '#e0b090']] }];\n  const SPEED = 92, AI_SPEED = 86, KICK_CD = .3;\n  const BALL = E.sprite(['.www.', 'wwkww', 'wkkkw', 'wwkww', '.www.'], { w: '#f4f4f0', k: '#2a2a30' });\n  const BALL2 = E.sprite(['.www.', 'wkwkw', 'wwwww', 'wkwkw', '.www.'], { w: '#f4f4f0', k: '#2a2a30' });\n  const SOUNDS = {\n    kick: { wave: 'noise', freq: 900, to: 200, dur: .07, vol: .3, filter: 'lowpass' }, thump: { wave: 'sine', freq: 120, to: 70, dur: .08, vol: .3 },\n    whistle: { wave: 'square', freq: 2200, vib: [30, .05], dur: .32, vol: .14 }, post: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 1400, to: 1100, dur: .3, vol: .25 },\n    crowd: { wave: 'noise', freq: 600, to: 900, dur: 1.4, vol: .18, filter: 'lowpass' }, slide: { wave: 'noise', freq: 400, to: 200, dur: .25, vol: .18 }\n  };\n  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(SOUNDS)) A.define(k, v);\n  const SONG = { bpm: 140, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the cage: a bright chant over a bouncing bass\n    { wave: 'square', vol: .07, notes: 'E5 . E5 G5 . E5 D5 . | C5 . C5 E5 . C5 B4 . | A4 . C5 . E5 . A5 . | G5 - - . . . . .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . | A2 . E2 . A2 . E2 . | F2 . C3 . F2 . C3 . | G2 . D3 . G2 . B2 .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . h . s . h k | k . h . s h h .' }] };\n\n  /* ---- THE STATE ---- */\n  let mode = 'menu', vs = false, team = [], all = [], ball = null, owner = null, last = null, clock = 0, half = 1, score = [0, 0], kickT = 0, t = 0, scripted = false;\n  let stats = null, curlT = 0, golden = false, restartBy = 0, over = false, kickHold = 0;   // kickHold: the kickoff's rule (the other side out of the circle) until the ball is played\n  const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['MATCH', 'VERSUS (2-4 PLAYERS)', 'BACK'], { onPick: i => i === 2 ? game.go('title') : i === 1 ? versus() : start(false) });\n  const after = new E.Menu(game, ['REMATCH', 'MENU'], { y: 150, onPick: i => i === 0 ? start(vs) : toMenu() });\n  const talk = new E.Dialog(game, { lines: 2, place: 'bottom', border: '#e8c070' });   // (at the bottom: clear of the score and of the touch buttons)\n  const VOICE = new E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, hat: 'band', colors: { cloth: '#3a3a4a', hair: '#5a3a2a', skin: '#e0b090', hat: '#2a2a30' } });\n  const say = text => { if (!scripted) talk.say(text, { name: 'CAGE RADIO', auto: 2.2, modal: false, alpha: .8, portrait: VOICE, portraitOpts: { zoom: 3, turn: .4 } }); };\n\n  function toMenu() { mode = 'menu'; game.splitScreen(0); game.allowJoin(false); A.music('title'); menu.i = 0; }\n  function versus() { vs = true; mode = 'join'; game.allowJoin({ max: 4 }); A.sfx('select'); }\n  /** a match: the four on the pitch, the ball at the centre, the clock at 0; players: who holds which (the inputs) */\n  function start(versus) {\n    vs = versus; map = map || makeMap(); score = [0, 0]; clock = 0; half = 1; golden = false; over = false; owner = null; last = null;\n    stats = { passes: 0, done: 0, shots: 0, lobs: 0, tackles: 0, goals: [], walls: 0, curled: 0 };\n    all = []; team = [[], []];\n    TEAMS.forEach((tm, s) => tm.players.forEach(([name, hair, skin], k) => {\n      const b = new E.Body({ x: CX, y: CY, r: 5, friction: 0, gravity: 700 });\n      const p = { side: s, k, name, body: b, rig: new E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, build: 'heroic', size: 1.05, hair: k ? 'spiky' : 'short', colors: Object.assign({ hair, skin }, tm.colors), speedRef: 80 }),\n        input: null, facing: s ? PI : 0, kick: null, slide: 0, stun: 0, cool: 0, meter: 0, charging: false, cheer: 0 };\n      team[s].push(p); all.push(p);\n    }));\n    // who holds whom: player 1 the GULLS' first (and, alone, whichever GULL is nearer the ball); in versus 2 the RUST, 3 and 4\n    // the second of each side\n    const P = game.players;\n    team[0][0].input = P[0];\n    if (vs) { if (P[1]) team[1][0].input = P[1]; if (P[2]) team[0][1].input = P[2]; if (P[3]) team[1][1].input = P[3]; }\n    ball = new E.Body({ x: CX, y: CY, r: 3, friction: 0, bounce: .55, gravity: 600 }); ball.spin = 0; ball.roll = 0;\n    kickoff(0); game.allowJoin(false); A.music(SONG); game.input.consumeAll();\n    game.follow(ball, { z: 8, lead: 10 }); game.cam.smooth = .18; game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v);\n    say('THE GULLS AGAINST THE RUST IN THE CAGE. HERE WE GO!');\n  }\n  /** the formation's spots: kicking off (s kicks), or in play (a team's two by where the ball is and who has it) */\n  const goalX = s => s ? X0 : X1;   // where side s shoots (the GULLS attack the right end)\n  function kickoff(s) {\n    owner = null; ball.x = CX; ball.y = CY; ball.z = 0; ball.onGround = true; ball.vx = ball.vy = ball.vz = 0; ball.spin = 0;\n    for (const p of all) {\n      const dir = p.side ? 1 : -1, b = p.body;\n      b.x = p.side === s && p.k === 0 ? CX + dir * 8 : CX + dir * (p.k ? 150 : 60); b.y = p.side === s && p.k === 0 ? CY : CY + (p.k ? 40 : -40) * (p.side ? -1 : 1);\n      b.vx = b.vy = 0; b.z = 0; p.facing = p.side ? PI : 0; p.kick = null; p.slide = 0; p.stun = 0; p.meter = 0; p.charging = false;\n    }\n    mode = 'kickoff'; kickT = 1; restartBy = s;\n  }\n  /** a player's spot in the formation now: with the ball (or near it), go for it; else, attacking, ahead on the far\n   *  side; defending, between the ball and its own goal */\n  function spot(p) {\n    const s = p.side, mate = team[s][1 - p.k], dir = s ? -1 : 1, has = owner && owner.side === s;\n    if (has) return [clamp(ball.x + dir * 90, X0 + 30, X1 - 30), CY + (ball.y < CY ? 60 : -60)];\n    const own = goalX(1 - s), near = Math.hypot(p.body.x - ball.x, p.body.y - ball.y) <= Math.hypot(mate.body.x - ball.x, mate.body.y - ball.y);\n    if (near) return [ball.x, ball.y];\n    return [lerp(ball.x, own, .55), lerp(ball.y, CY, .5)];\n  }\n\n  /* ---- THE BALL: owned (at its owner's feet), or loose: a Body that rolls, bounces off the ground and the boards and\n   * curls by its spin; a goal, over the bar, out of the cage ---- */\n  function ballStep(dt) {\n    if (owner) {\n      const b = owner.body, f = owner.facing; ball.x = b.x + Math.cos(f) * 7; ball.y = b.y + Math.sin(f) * 7; ball.z = 0; ball.onGround = true;\n      ball.vx = b.vx; ball.vy = b.vy; ball.vz = 0; ball.roll += Math.hypot(b.vx, b.vy) * dt; return;\n    }\n    const vx0 = ball.vx, vy0 = ball.vy, sp = Math.hypot(ball.vx, ball.vy);\n    if (ball.spin && sp > 20) { const k = ball.spin * dt; ball.vx += -vy0 / sp * k * sp; ball.vy += vx0 / sp * k * sp; ball.spin *= Math.exp(-dt * 1.4); }   // curl: across its path\n    if (ball.z <= .5) { const f = Math.exp(-dt * 1.1); ball.vx *= f; ball.vy *= f; }   // rolling slows it\n    ball.update(dt, map);   // (the Body bounces off the boards and the ground by its bounce)\n    if (ball.hitWall) { ball.spin = 0; stats.walls++; if (Math.hypot(vx0, vy0) > 60) A.sfx('thump'); }\n    if (ball.bounced) A.sfx('thump');\n    ball.roll += Math.hypot(ball.vx, ball.vy) * dt;\n    // a goal: over the line between the posts and under the bar; over it, a goal kick; out of the cage, thrown back in\n    for (const s of [0, 1]) {\n      const gx = goalX(s), past = s ? ball.x < gx - 2 : ball.x > gx + 2;\n      if (past && Math.abs(ball.y - CY) < GH && ball.z < BAR) return goal(s);\n      if (past && (ball.z >= BAR || Math.abs(ball.y - CY) >= GH)) return restart(1 - s, s ? X0 + 24 : X1 - 24, CY, 'OVER THE BAR. A GOAL KICK');\n    }\n    if (ball.x < X0 - 40 || ball.x > X1 + 40 || ball.y < Y0 - 4 || ball.y > Y1 + 4) restart(last ? 1 - last.side : 0, clamp(ball.x, X0 + 12, X1 - 12), clamp(ball.y, Y0 + 12, Y1 - 12), 'OUT OF THE CAGE! THROWN BACK IN');\n  }\n  /** play goes on from (x, y) with the ball at the feet of side s's nearer player */\n  function restart(s, x, y, line) {\n    const p = team[s].slice().sort((a, b) => Math.hypot(a.body.x - x, a.body.y - y) - Math.hypot(b.body.x - x, b.body.y - y))[0];\n    p.body.x = x - (s ? -8 : 8); p.body.y = y; p.facing = s ? PI : 0; owner = p; ball.spin = 0; A.sfx('whistle'); if (line) say(line);\n  }\n  function goal(s) {\n    score[s]++; stats.goals.push([s, last ? last.name : '?', Math.round(clock)]); owner = null; mode = 'goal'; kickT = 2.4; restartBy = 1 - s;\n    for (const p of team[s]) p.cheer = 2.4; game.shake(3); A.sfx('crowd'); A.sfx('whistle');\n    P.sparks(ball.x, ball.y, 16, 16, null, { color: '#ffe08a' }); P.ring(ball.x, ball.y, 4, 34, '#fff6c0', .5);\n    say(golden ? 'GOLDEN GOAL! ' + (last ? last.name : '') + ' WINS IT FOR THE ' + TEAMS[s].name + '!' : 'GOAL! ' + (last ? last.name + ' SCORES FOR THE ' : 'THE ') + TEAMS[s].name + '! ' + score[0] + ' - ' + score[1]);\n    if (golden) { over = true; }\n  }\n\n  /* ---- KICKS: a pass along the ground led to the teammate, a lob over by E.arc, a shot from the meter with aftertouch ---- */\n  /** the teammate a pass goes to: the one the stick points at (within 70 degrees), else the other */\n  const mateOf = p => team[p.side][1 - p.k];\n  function pass(p) {\n    const m = mateOf(p), b = p.body, d = Math.hypot(m.body.x - b.x, m.body.y - b.y), sp = clamp(d * 1.5 + 90, 150, 270), lead = d / sp;\n    const tx = m.body.x + m.body.vx * lead * .8, ty = m.body.y + m.body.vy * lead * .8, a = Math.atan2(ty - b.y, tx - b.x);\n    release(p, Math.cos(a) * sp, Math.sin(a) * sp, 0); stats.passes++; ball.to = m;\n  }\n  function lob(p) {\n    const m = mateOf(p), lead = .55, tx = m.body.x + m.body.vx * lead, ty = m.body.y + m.body.vy * lead;\n    const v = E.arc({ x: ball.x, y: ball.y, z: 0 }, { x: tx, y: ty, z: 0 }, ball.gravity, { apex: 30 });\n    release(p, v.vx, v.vy, v.vz); stats.lobs++; stats.passes++; ball.to = m;\n  }\n  /** a shot: power from the meter (0..1), aimed across the goal mouth by the stick's up and down */\n  function shoot(p, power, aimY) {\n    const gx = goalX(p.side), gy = CY + clamp(aimY, -1, 1) * (GH -","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-build--20261104-055947--x9a2bbb-work/e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa/tool-results/bxjpl01e9.txt","persistedOutputSize":34810},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017MucYqneKYGcwpDGxngvMU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
