{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghyYqH1RzUET9Hp2bBbC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cp2nVHu7FZj1tygkX11pHD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055947__x9a2bbb/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ndoc = {\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:59:47\",\n    \"source\": \"ice hockey (over the top arcade style)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md (the plan given with this build)\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade sports: three-a-side hockey with goalies, a Cup Run story, exhibition and practice\",\n    \"perspective\": \"TV broadcast camera (threequarter, 2.5D) with an overhead view (V)\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (handoff package), plain JavaScript; Node 24 for headless tests; Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium for the browser smoke test\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's PS1-era pixel art and humanoid rigs; hockey gear, rink, nets and crowd drawn in code\",\n    \"animation\": \"The engine's procedural humanoid rig and poses (skating, cheer, stagger, down, save)\",\n    \"audio\": \"All synthesized in code: chip sound effects, babble voices in Animalese style, one match song\",\n    \"online\": \"none (AI Hub session not built)\",\n    \"testing\": \"one command (tests/run.mjs): headless Node checks and a Chromium smoke test, printing failures and a count\",\n    \"research\": \"none\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium, headless, through Playwright\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"11 issues found during testing.\",\n    \"4 were game-breaking: a hang in an angle wrap, goalies going NaN from a duplicated data key (and an unset target), the net box blocking every goal, and a draw crash that only the browser run caught.\",\n    \"Most helpful: headless match runs that counted shots, saves, goals and goal-line crossings. They exposed the net and goalie bugs.\",\n    \"Least helpful: scene checks that only confirm the scene name. Headless runs skip drawing, so they passed while a draw crashed.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Most liked: the sports kit as a base, the TileMap with runtime cell changes (map.set for broken glass), and game.advance for headless play.\",\n    \"Stuck or guessed wrong: the pixel fonts had no PlayStation symbols; E.store needs localStorage (stubbed in the tests); the Dialog voice option and the mouse-aim call were taken from the docs and not fully verified.\",\n    \"Most important thing built myself: the rink's collision (a wall grid from the rounded rectangle), the puck and goal-line rules, and the skater and goalie AI.\",\n    \"Hardest: finding the right call in a 14,700-line engine file, and that headless runs skip drawing, so draw bugs need a browser.\",\n    \"Engine change: PlayStation symbols added to both pixel fonts (they drew as ?). Logged in ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\",\n    \"One change: run scene drawing in headless mode (or offer a draw-check mode) so screen code can be tested without a browser.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"Liked most: the explicit rules (one test command, no subagents, file names and sections) and the plan's numbers.\",\n    \"Confusing: the title rule (TASK asks for 50 random titles, STAGE says use the plan's title), and a 1,500-line plan for a medium-effort build.\",\n    \"Hardest: fitting the full plan into one build (online play, seven drills, AI tuning without watching the play live).\",\n    \"Would change: name a minimum vertical slice and what can be cut, and say whether online play must work for the game to count as done.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Ice Hoc-Kaboom\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Three a side. Goalies. Glass. KABOOM.\",\n    \"description\": \"Three-a-side arcade hockey with goalies, breakable glass, fights and a KABOOM mode, plus a five-game Cup Run and exhibition matches.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"ice hockey\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Move: left stick or WASD; Pass J / X; Shoot K / Square (hold for slapshot); Deke L; Lob I; Turbo Shift; KABOOM B\",\n    \"tags\": [\"arcade\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"pixel art\", \"story\"]\n  }\n}\njson.dump(doc, open('exit-interview.json', 'w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\njson.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\nprint('exit-interview.json parses; keys:', list(doc.keys()))\nEOF\nls -la /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055947__x9a2bbb/work/ | head -20","description":"Write exit-interview.json and check it parses"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2856,"cache_read_input_tokens":382997,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2856},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa","uuid":"c4888e50-b3bd-4b74-8529-9636a4a3cb4e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:35:29.022Z","request_id":"req_011CghyYpth4mio4uXnwMpwA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Cp2nVHu7FZj1tygkX11pHD":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055947__x9a2bbb/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ndoc = {\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:59:47\",\n    \"source\": \"ice hockey (over the top arcade style)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md (the plan given with this build)\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade sports: three-a-side hockey with goalies, a Cup Run story, exhibition and practice\",\n    \"perspective\": \"TV broadcast camera (threequarter, 2.5D) with an overhead view (V)\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (handoff package), plain JavaScript; Node 24 for headless tests; Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium for the browser smoke test\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's PS1-era pixel art and humanoid rigs; hockey gear, rink, nets and crowd drawn in code\",\n    \"animation\": \"The engine's procedural humanoid rig and poses (skating, cheer, stagger, down, save)\",\n    \"audio\": \"All synthesized in code: chip sound effects, babble voices in Animalese style, one match song\",\n    \"online\": \"none (AI Hub session not built)\",\n    \"testing\": \"one command (tests/run.mjs): headless Node checks and a Chromium smoke test, printing failures and a count\",\n    \"research\": \"none\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium, headless, through Playwright\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"11 issues found during testing.\",\n    \"4 were game-breaking: a hang in an angle wrap, goalies going NaN from a duplicated data key (and an unset target), the net box blocking every goal, and a draw crash that only the browser run caught.\",\n    \"Most helpful: headless match runs that counted shots, saves, goals and goal-line crossings. They exposed the net and goalie bugs.\",\n    \"Least helpful: scene checks that only confirm the scene name. Headless runs skip drawing, so they passed while a draw crashed.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Most liked: the sports kit as a base, the TileMap with runtime cell changes (map.set for broken glass), and game.advance for headless play.\",\n    \"Stuck or guessed wrong: the pixel fonts had no PlayStation symbols; E.store needs localStorage (stubbed in the tests); the Dialog voice option and the mouse-aim call were taken from the docs and not fully verified.\",\n    \"Most important thing built myself: the rink's collision (a wall grid from the rounded rectangle), the puck and goal-line rules, and the skater and goalie AI.\",\n    \"Hardest: finding the right call in a 14,700-line engine file, and that headless runs skip drawing, so draw bugs need a browser.\",\n    \"Engine change: PlayStation symbols added to both pixel fonts (they drew as ?). Logged in ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\",\n    \"One change: run scene drawing in headless mode (or offer a draw-check mode) so screen code can be tested without a browser.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"Liked most: the explicit rules (one test command, no subagents, file names and sections) and the plan's numbers.\",\n    \"Confusing: the title rule (TASK asks for 50 random titles, STAGE says use the plan's title), and a 1,500-line plan for a medium-effort build.\",\n    \"Hardest: fitting the full plan into one build (online play, seven drills, AI tuning without watching the play live).\",\n    \"Would change: name a minimum vertical slice and what can be cut, and say whether online play must work for the game to count as done.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Ice Hoc-Kaboom\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Three a side. Goalies. Glass. KABOOM.\",\n    \"description\": \"Three-a-side arcade hockey with goalies, breakable glass, fights and a KABOOM mode, plus a five-game Cup Run and exhibition matches.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"ice hockey\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Move: left stick or WASD; Pass J / X; Shoot K / Square (hold for slapshot); Deke L; Lob I; Turbo Shift; KABOOM B\",\n    \"tags\": [\"arcade\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"pixel art\", \"story\"]\n  }\n}\njson.dump(doc, open('exit-interview.json', 'w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\njson.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\nprint('exit-interview.json parses; keys:', list(doc.keys()))\nEOF\nls -la /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055