{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1o1v6xg7BkviBQporB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop hook's specific gaps are closed, but I can't honestly say every feature in the plan is built, so the goal's condition is still not met. The part that remains is listed below.\n\n**Closed in this pass**\n- **Title:** I did the 50-title brainstorm myself and drew with `secrets.randbelow(50)+1`. The draw gave 11, so the game is now **Ice Breakers**. The HTML, the dev folder, the exit interview and the title screen are all renamed.\n- **Fights (plan 7.11):** balance and stamina for both fighters, with stamina regeneration. Four moves with the plan's timings: jab, haymaker (wind-up, whiff opens the fighter), duck, yank (breaks the guard, and three yanks in four seconds pull the jersey over the head and blind the rival). Challenges need a grudge of 40 and a half-second hold of lob. A CPU accepts with the plan's formula, and a human rival has three seconds to press lob. A turtle costs BOOM. The loser goes to the sin bin for 20 seconds, and the other side gets a POWER PLAY line. Time-up is a draw with no penalty.\n- **KABOOM (plan 7.10):** a full meter starts KABOOM automatically for 15 seconds, and the other side's goal ends it. It gives infinite turbo and doubles slapshot charge speed. A full charge fires a 760-unit KABOOM shot with zero error, which blasts a goalie, knocks down a skater, and breaks glass. The goalie reacts 0.03 s faster. BOOM gains follow the plan's list where the game has the event: checks, saves, shots on goal, completed passes, chirps, fights and goals.\n- **Overhead camera:** V cycles the views, and a browser check confirms it changes the view.\n- **About/Credits:** five pages with the full Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt feedback, wrapped to fit.\n- **Touch notice:** I captured a screenshot. The notice reads \"Controller or keyboard required\", with SETTINGS below it. The menu had overlapped the notice, so I moved it.\n- **Boss:** the Cup Run's final rival goalie is quicker and bigger, with a boss banner.\n\n**Still not built (so the goal stays unmet)**\n- Plan 7.12: fan throws, power-ups (BOOM Box, Lumber and the rest) and arena hazards (thin ice, the mascot, the Discount Drop).\n- The Flood Wagon intermission minigame (plan 7.10–7.17 references).\n- Plan BOOM sources not in the game: the mascot, the perfect Flood Wagon, and Doris's organ.\n- The boss is a stronger goalie, not the plan's multi-phase fight.\n- Online play has been run only through the hub's harness, which passes.\n\n**Verification:** `node tests/run.mjs` passes 66 of 66 checks. They cover the headless simulation, the browser smoke test (every scene, real key input, Dev Mode from the pause menu, the V camera, keyboard join, the touch device and a fight drawn), and the AI Hub harness for 2 and 4 players with latency, a server host and a host who leaves.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 05:59:47\n- Source: ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: sports, three-a-side with goalies; Cup Run, exhibition, practice, online sessions\n- Perspective: TV broadcast camera (threequarter, 2.5D); overhead on V; brawler in fights\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Node 24, Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium\n- Art direction: the engine's PS1-era pixel art and humanoid rigs; hockey gear, rink, crowd and effects in code\n- Animation: the engine's procedural rig and poses\n- Audio: all synthesized in code\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1 to 4 seats\n- Testing: one command, `tests/run.mjs`\n- Research: none\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium, headless\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found in the game build: 11.\n- Critical or game-breaking: 4. A hang in an angle wrap, goalies going NaN from a duplicated data key, the net box blocking every goal, and a draw crash that only the browser run caught.\n- Most helpful: headless match runs that counted shots, saves, goals and goal-line crossings.\n- Least helpful: scene checks that only confirm the scene name, because headless runs skip drawing.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Most liked: the sports kit as a base, TileMap runtime cell changes, and `game.advance` for headless play.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: the pixel fonts had no PlayStation symbols; `E.store` needs `localStorage`, which I stubbed in tests; the Dialog voice option came from the docs.\n- Built myself: the rink collision, the puck and goal-line rules, the skater and goalie AI, the fights, KABOOM and the session netcode.\n- Hardest: finding the right calls in a 14,700-line file, and that headless runs skip drawing.\n- Engine changes: PlayStation symbols in both pixel fonts, and the hub's Create + Options rule, logged in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n- One change I'd make: run scene drawing headless, or offer a draw-check mode.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the explicit rules (one test command, no subagents, file names and sections) and the plan's numbers.\n- Confusing: TASK.md asks for 50 random titles while STAGE.md says to use the plan's title, and the plan is large for a medium-effort build.\n- Hardest: fitting the full plan into one build, and tuning AI play without watching it live.\n- Would change: name a minimum slice and what can be cut, and say whether online play must work for the game to count as done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1584,"cache_read_input_tokens":533462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1584},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null