{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3czLo4GKH3YPRUQx1e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan's named systems are now built and tested, but the goal's \"every feature\" condition still isn't fully met. A few smaller plan items remain, listed below. I'm not claiming completion.\n\n**Built in this pass**\n- **Fan throws (7.12):** every 25–45 seconds of play, plus a 25% chance after a big hit or goal. Items arc onto the neutral or attacking zone, slide to a stop, and last 12 seconds, blinking for the last 3. A skater within 12 takes the item, and its timer shows over their head.\n- **Power-ups:** HOT SAUCE (infinite turbo, 8 s), GRANDMA'S TAPE (10 s; can't lose the puck to checks below a big hit), POUTINE (10 s; can't be knocked down and checks hit 1.6×), LUMBER (next 3 shots +30% speed, no error), BRICK PADS (the team's goalie ×1.35 for 12 s), BOOM BOX (+40 BOOM), HOT COCOA (pond only; 8 s of +20% speed and a full refill).\n- **Item greed:** a CPU skater not in the play goes for a power-up within 120.\n- **Hazards:**\n  - Octopus (Lumber Yard): a slip patch after goals, picked up at the next stoppage.\n  - Rubber rat (Lumber Yard): a moving slip, 10 s.\n  - Hat trick: a third goal makes the stands throw hats.\n  - Thin ice (pond): three patches with integrity. A knockdown costs 50 and a big hit there 100. At 0 it becomes a hole that freezes skaters for 3 s, swallows a puck (faceoff), and refreezes after 30 s.\n  - Snowbank boards (pond): a big hit near the boards buries the skater, and the puck bounces less.\n  - Polar Pete (Dome): the mascot skates figure eights and can be checked (MASCOT DOWN, BOOM +10). He gets up after 3 s and waves.\n  - Discount Drop (Dome): a crate falls to centre ice every 40 s and breaks into a random power-up.\n- **Flood Wagon (intermission):** a playable resurfacing lap with steering. Perfect is 90% or more (BOOM +30). The skip runs the AI's lap at 70%, which is never perfect. A steering-route check shows a perfect lap is reachable.\n- **BOOM sources:** the Flood Wagon's perfect lap, the mascot knockdown, and Doris's organ (+30 per goal, in the Vault, the chapter 5 arena).\n- **KABOOM and fights** were already built from the previous pass.\n- **Session sync:** items, the mascot, the octopus and the thin ice are sent to online clients.\n\n**Verification:** `node tests/run.mjs` passes 73 of 73 checks. The browser checks draw all five arenas, the flood scene and a fight. The hub harness passes all four rounds.\n\n**Still not built, so the goal stays unmet**\n- One-timer (+6) and deke-beat (+6) BOOM sources.\n- The Flood Wagon \"Ask / Always / Never\" setting. It runs whenever a human is playing a non-session match, and the skip is immediate rather than a 6-second fast-forward.\n- The pond's boards still look like glass. Only the bounce and the burying are snowbank-like.\n- The mascot's mass isn't modelled (he only pushes skaters out of the way).\n- The Gilded Mode for the final, and the cheat octopus.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 05:59:47\n- Source: ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: sports, three-a-side with goalies; Cup Run, exhibition, practice, online sessions\n- Perspective: TV broadcast camera (threequarter, 2.5D); overhead on V; brawler in fights\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Node 24, Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium\n- Art direction: the engine's PS1-era pixel art and humanoid rigs; hockey gear, rink, crowd, hazards and effects in code\n- Animation: the engine's procedural rig and poses\n- Audio: all synthesized in code\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1 to 4 seats\n- Testing: one command, `tests/run.mjs`\n- Research: none\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium, headless\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found in the game build: 11.\n- Critical or game-breaking: 4. A hang in an angle wrap, goalies going NaN from a duplicated data key, the net box blocking every goal, and a draw crash that only the browser run caught.\n- Most helpful: headless match runs that counted shots, saves, goals and goal-line crossings.\n- Least helpful: scene checks that only confirm the scene name, because headless runs skip drawing.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Most liked: the sports kit as a base, TileMap runtime cell changes, and `game.advance` for headless play.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: the pixel fonts had no PlayStation symbols, `E.store` needs `localStorage` (given a fake in the tests), and the Dialog voice option came from the docs.\n- Built myself: the rink collision, the puck and goal-line rules, the AI, the fights, KABOOM, the items and hazards, the Flood Wagon, and the session netcode.\n- Hardest: finding the right calls in a 14,700-line file, and that headless runs skip drawing.\n- Engine changes: PlayStation symbols in both pixel fonts, and the hub's Create + Options rule, logged in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n- One change I'd make: run scene drawing headless, or offer a draw-check mode.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the explicit rules (one test command, no subagents, file names and sections) and the plan's numbers.\n- Confusing: TASK.md asks for 50 random titles while STAGE.md says to use the plan's title, and the plan is large for a medium-effort build.\n- Hardest: fitting the full plan into one build, and tuning AI play without watching it live.\n- Would change: name a minimum slice and what can be cut, and say whether online play must work for the game to count as done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_read_input_tokens":606731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa","uuid":"09b67f44-2d0d-4de5-a2f1-b19d91bba081","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:28:46.315Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3cyyiKiX3FMZu1Gqhq"}
