{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4UzpDXEqbiX3Sqx9Vm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 75 checks pass. I'll stop here and be direct about the status. Everything in this pass is built and verified, but I can't honestly say the goal is met. The stop hook measures against the full plan, and the plan describes more than I've built.\n\n**Built in this pass**\n- **One-timers:** a receiver who fires as the pass arrives shoots faster with half the error, and the team gains 6 BOOM. CPU receivers do this too.\n- **Deke beats:** a deke that leaves its defender behind gives 6 BOOM, once per deke.\n- **Flood Wagon setting:** Ask / Always / Never in the Settings menu. Ask asks at each intermission. Never skips the minigame. A skip now runs the AI driver for its last six seconds, and a declined lap is no resurfacing.\n- **Gilded Mode:** in the final, the rival's KABOOM is gold: the banner, the sparks, the puck trail.\n- **Mascot mass:** Polar Pete takes knockback from checks (mass 1.5) and slides back to his figure-eight path.\n- **Cheat octopus:** a Dev Mode row puts a slip patch on the ice.\n- **Glass cracks:** a first hit cracks a panel (BOOM +8). A hard hit or a second hit shatters it (BOOM +15).\n- **Smaller details:** POUTINE makes every check a big hit; GRANDMA'S TAPE stops other sides taking a taped skater's pass; HOT SAUCE has a fire trail; the pond's snowbanks are white.\n\n**Verified:** `node tests/run.mjs` passes 75 of 75 checks. Those include a Flood Wagon lap that reaches 90% with a route bot, and the Ask prompt waiting for input.\n\n**Still not built from the plan**\n- Instant replay and the broadcast camera's punch-ins and framing (plan 7.15–7.16).\n- Player intros, chirp bubbles over heads (chirps are booth lines only), and crowd waves and signs.\n- The organ's own sound and the crowd bed beyond the basics.\n- The shootout is resolved by odds, not played out with the goalie as the plan describes.\n- The goalie is not manually controllable.\n- Team AI roles are simpler than the plan's.\n- The story's scripted cutscenes with portraits (chapters are text cards and choices).\n- The animation lab.\n- The glass visuals for cracks are not shown; only the BOOM and the state change.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 05:59:47\n- Source: ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: sports, three-a-side with goalies; Cup Run, exhibition, practice, online sessions\n- Perspective: TV broadcast camera (threequarter, 2.5D); overhead on V; brawler in fights\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Node 24, Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium\n- Art direction: the engine's PS1-era pixel art and humanoid rigs; hockey gear, rink, crowd, hazards and effects in code\n- Animation: the engine's procedural rig and poses\n- Audio: all synthesized in code\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1 to 4 seats\n- Testing: one command, `tests/run.mjs`\n- Research: none\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium, headless\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found in the game build: 11.\n- Critical or game-breaking: 4. A hang in an angle wrap, goalies going NaN from a duplicated data key, the net box blocking every goal, and a draw crash that only the browser run caught.\n- Most helpful: headless match runs that counted shots, saves, goals and goal-line crossings.\n- Least helpful: scene checks that only confirm the scene name, because headless runs skip drawing.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Most liked: the sports kit as a base, TileMap runtime cell changes, and `game.advance` for headless play.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: the pixel fonts had no PlayStation symbols; `E.store` needs `localStorage` (given a fake in the tests); the Dialog voice option came from the docs.\n- Built myself: the rink collision, the puck and goal-line rules, the AI, the fights, KABOOM, items and hazards, the Flood Wagon, and the session netcode.\n- Hardest: finding the right calls in a 14,700-line file, and that headless runs skip drawing.\n- Engine changes: PlayStation symbols in both pixel fonts, and the hub's Create + Options rule, logged in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n- One change I'd make: run scene drawing headless, or offer a draw-check mode.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the explicit rules (one test command, no subagents, file names and sections) and the plan's numbers.\n- Confusing: TASK.md asks for 50 random titles while STAGE.md says to use the plan's title, and the plan is large for a medium-effort build.\n- Hardest: fitting the full plan into one build, and tuning AI play without watching it live.\n- Would change: name a minimum slice and what can be cut, and say whether online play must work for the game to count as done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":643,"cache_read_input_tokens":635422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":643},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa","uuid":"c0478d66-85f5-43af-b211-369fc2e839d0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:40:10.911Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4UzQA9Yzxx2XCWco7k"}
