{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5E9xLwtDBupiSx5q4p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop hook's list is now built, but the goal still isn't fully met, and I won't claim it is.\n\n**Built in this pass (plan sections in brackets)**\n- **Played-out shootout (7.14):** three shots each, home first, then sudden death. Each attempt has an 8-second clock and ends on a shot, a save, a goal, or the puck going off the ice. A human shooter uses the stick and shoot button. A human on the defending side moves the goalie along the line with the stick.\n- **Instant replay (7.16):** after a goal, the last few seconds replay at half speed, then the real positions come back.\n- **Broadcast punch-ins (7.15):** a big hit pushes the camera in briefly.\n- **Chirp bubbles (7.9):** a chirp shows as a bubble over the chirper.\n- **Player intros (7.17):** the booth introduces the players at the first faceoff.\n- **Crowd waves and signs (7.17):** a goal or big hit starts a wave through the stands, and some fans hold signs.\n- **Cutscene portraits (11.3):** each chapter's cutscene shows your goalie and the rival's, drawn by the engine's rig.\n- **Animation lab (15):** every pose and attack of the rig, one after another, with Next and Previous. It opens from Dev Mode, or at `#lab`.\n\n**Verified:** `node tests/run.mjs` passes 76 of 76 checks. The browser checks draw the lab and the cutscene. I looked at a cutscene screenshot and fixed the text overlapping the portraits.\n\n**Still not built, so the goal is not met**\n- **Team AI (7.13):** the formation roles (centre, wing, defence) and the chaser exist. The plan's reaction-time cadence, the difficulty curves and the per-role decisions do not.\n- **Broadcast director (7.15):** the punch-in is the only camera move. The plan's follow, lead and framing rules for fights, replays and intros are not built.\n- **Commentary and intros (7.17):** the booth draws from pools of lines. The plan's per-event coverage and the intros' on/off option are not complete.\n- **Options (11.x, 13):** the plan's Player intros on/off, Replays Auto/Off, and the flood Ask/Always/Never were only partly wired. Intros and replays have no settings yet.\n- **Smaller plan details:** the pond's glass-free boards, and the mascot's collision shape, are approximations.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 05:59:47\n- Source: ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: sports, three-a-side with goalies; Cup Run, exhibition, practice, online sessions\n- Perspective: TV broadcast camera (threequarter, 2.5D); overhead on V; brawler in fights\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2, AI Hub session.js 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Node 24, Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium\n- Art direction: the engine's PS1-era pixel art and humanoid rigs; hockey gear, rink, crowd, hazards and effects in code\n- Animation: the engine's procedural rig and poses; the lab shows every one\n- Audio: all synthesized in code\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1 to 4 seats\n- Testing: one command, `tests/run.mjs`\n- Research: none\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium, headless\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found in the game build: 11.\n- Critical or game-breaking: 4. A hang in an angle wrap, goalies going NaN from a duplicated data key, the net box blocking every goal, and a draw crash that only the browser run caught.\n- Most helpful: headless match runs that counted shots, saves, goals and goal-line crossings.\n- Least helpful: scene checks that only confirm the scene name, because headless runs skip drawing.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Most liked: the sports kit as a base, TileMap runtime cell changes, and `game.advance` for headless play.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: the pixel fonts had no PlayStation symbols; `E.store` needs `localStorage` (given a fake in the tests); the Dialog voice option came from the docs.\n- Built myself: the rink collision, the puck and goal-line rules, the AI, the fights, KABOOM, items and hazards, the Flood Wagon, the shootout, the replay, and the session netcode.\n- Hardest: finding the right calls in a 14,700-line file, and that headless runs skip drawing.\n- Engine changes: PlayStation symbols in both pixel fonts, and the hub's Create + Options rule, logged in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n- One change I'd make: run scene drawing headless, or offer a draw-check mode.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the explicit rules (one test command, no subagents, file names and sections) and the plan's numbers.\n- Confusing: TASK.md asks for 50 random titles while STAGE.md says to use the plan's title, and the plan is large for a medium-effort build.\n- Hardest: fitting the full plan into one build, and tuning AI play without watching it live.\n- Would change: name a minimum slice and what can be cut, and say whether the plan's full detail counts as \"every feature\" for done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":871,"cache_read_input_tokens":670555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":871},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e95508dc-65c4-494d-9367-fd17dc92e8aa","uuid":"d9bcc25c-1895-4dcb-a407-9269f8be2a8f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:49:49.336Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5E9WoTrNJYeEWVr9cn"}
